# Ruleset: Tailscale direct
#
# Expects DIRECT. Must follow Coordination.list.
#
# The process rules cover the gateway's own client, which dials DERP relays by bare address: 2,425 such flows rode the fallthrough proxy in the 14 days to 2026-09-09.
#
# The DERP relays double as STUN servers, so proxying them makes Tailscale advertise the proxy's address as its own endpoint. That defeats NAT traversal and pins every peer to relay. The guard that enforces this for the STUN port is a logical rule and cannot live in a rule set, so it stays inline in the profile:
#
#   AND,((PROTOCOL,UDP),(DEST-PORT,3478)),DIRECT
#
# Only the DERP relay names are pinned here. The website, pkgs.tailscale.com and log.tailscale.com are ordinary HTTPS that is slow on the direct path: measured 2026-10-30, tailscale.com/download took 1.1 to 2.3 s direct against 0.1 to 0.3 s through a Hong Kong exit, and pkgs.tailscale.com 0.9 to 2.2 s against 0.7 to 1.7 s. They reach a proxy through FINAL.

DOMAIN-WILDCARD,derp*.tailscale.com
PROCESS-NAME,Tailscale
PROCESS-NAME,tailscaled
PROCESS-NAME,io.tailscale.ipn.macsys.network-extension
